dsv41 patch 0060 (20.10.2026): three kernel pages per manager block for the ratio-1 KV group. In use
(VLLM_DSV41_KV_PAIR=3). Base: the v9 files (0057 + 0059).
Why: with 0057 the ratio-1 group's paired block (2 x 46,080 = 92,160 B) still sits in the ratio-2 group's 138,240 B
block stride, so a third of each of its blocks stays empty. Three 64-state pages are 3 x 46,080 = 138,240 B, exactly the
stride (with 0059's NVFP4 records 3 x 33,280 = 99,840 B, again exactly the stride): no padding left.
How: VLLM_DSV41_KV_PAIR=3 gives the ratio-1 specs 192-token manager blocks (spec block size x 3, storage_block_size 64)
on top of 0057's paired-page machinery. vLLM's hybrid allocator takes it generically: the scheduler block is the lcm of
the group block sizes (384), the hash block their gcd (64), BlockTables expands manager blocks into kernel blocks
(b * k + j), the views divide by the ratio. One fix in kv_cache_interface.py: _apply_alignment_padding shrank a
deliberately larger page in replace() (a 192-state NVFP4 indexer page: 25,600 instead of 3 x 8,704 B); it now keeps a
larger page that is already aligned (no effect with FP8 records or VLLM_DSV41_KV_PAIR=1).
Per token and node, as charged for a max-length request: 1,800 B data (1,462.5 B fp8_ds_mla + 337.5 B indexer keys)
+ 829 B sliding-window admission reserve = 2,630 B (v5: 4,069 B incl. 1,440 B padding; 0057: 2,989 B).
Measured (21.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v12, 3.75 GiB KV pool per node, against a fresh start of the 0057
configuration): KV pool 1,346,928 -> 1,531,258 tokens (+13.7 %; offline harness: 1,531,258), bytes per token live
(250K-token prompt) 2,187 -> 1,827; cost per verify round -0.51 % (geometric mean of 14 cells, worst +1.4 %), tok/s
-0.03 %; T=0 texts identical 8/8; needles at 250K 6/6; corruption test (8K/30K/50K/100K, 4 each) 0 hits; lowest free
memory under load 1,992 MiB head / 3,480 MiB worker.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_KV_PAIR=3 (1 = 0057's two pages, 0 = off).
